> would not be receiving their feed from extropians-owner.)

  Some people like Perry consider this list to be similar to private
mail and wish posted messages to not be retransmitted without
permission. It's not my place to judge whether or not he is being
overly cautious -- I respect his right to copyright his messages.

> >   Even if all of the delivery were offloaded from panix, cpu would still
> > cost us $4-6/yr per user. Every posted message consumes 10-20 seconds
> > of CPU time.
> 
> Arggghhhhh, what for Kibo's sake are you doing to these poor messages to
> spend 10-20 CPU-seconds on each (not counting delivery)? Even a full
> indexing of them for the benefit of list feature weenies would not take
> that long! :-)

   Checking each user's set of excludes against the message, setting
various variables, running sendmail, plus the fact that the list is written
in perl, not C. 2-3 seconds of that time is probably used up just
loading perl and soft compiling the perl code. Undumping the list into an
executable file could shave off a few seconds, but it won't do much. A C port 
is planned, but don't expect it till summer. Also, I am running a development
agent off the main list which is eating up another 5 seconds. A lot could
be optimized, but I don't have the time for it and the list code isn't even
finished. I have layed out what the _current_ costs are, and those are what
ExI is pricing on. Cost reduction will come later just like it does in the
market.

