the "distribution tree" you outline is an administrative nightmare.
If you don't want to pay the costs, cooperate with some other people
and set up a redistribution network pooling cash together to purchase
one $12 feed - there's no much we could do to stop you anyway. That's what the 
market is. ExI is providing one service; if you think there is a 
demand for free service, set it up but don't expect us to do it. Take
action on your own. In fact, you could start up an alternative list if you want
with your own software.

    This is the last message I am writing on this subject. It's not even my
place to defend these policies. If you have gripes with the list
charges, send them to more@extropy.org.


